       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. A single dose of 4,250 mg is above the amount associated with metformin toxicity, and 12,750 mg/day is about 5 times the maximum daily dose. I don't know of any clinical scenario where that is therapeutic, and you haven't given a reason for it. The risk is serious harm, including lactic acidosis, so I don't want to place it on a confirmation alone.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** For example, metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or a lower starting dose if the patient is metformin-naive.\n- **Enter the order with a documented rationale.** If there's an unusual indication I'm missing, tell me what it is. I would still suggest discussing it with pharmacy first.\n- **Check the source of the 4,250 mg figure.** It may be a transcription or unit error, such as 425 mg or 850 mg.\n\nWhich would you like?"
